{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>לא אבה</b> — three times in the Masorah: one instance here, and the other two: לא אבה לי, לא אבה. The reading of יבמות (Yevamot 110a) cites לא אבה only from the yevamah passage, as it is written: 'For Israel and Judah are not widowed of their Elohim.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :register {:hand-fixed {:from "widowed of their God", :to "widowed of their Elohim", :by :shovel, :date "2026-07-12"}}, :notes {0 "The comment juxtaposes three Masoretic occurrences of לא אבה; the final scriptural quotation is from Jeremiah 51:5, where the word אלמן connects to the yevamah (levirate) context discussed in Yevamot 110a."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:25:21.802879467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}